/* book exam traps: Direct injection is not the same as direct control. Direct means the injector sprays into the cylinder; it does not mean a lever or human directly controls the fuel. | For a four-stroke engine, each cylinder injects once every two revolutions. Injections per cylinder per minute are rpm ÷ 2, not rpm. | Injection timing is the start of fuel delivery, not the spark timing; spark timing belongs to the ignition system (see Ignition timing and spark advance). | Solid injection and airless injection are the same thing. Air injection is the obsolete air-blast method, not a modern air-assisted petrol injector. | Injection lag is the delay before the nozzle opens; injection duration is the crank angle from opening to closing. Convert either with θ = 6Nt, not 360Nt. */
